 a good example of  someone who you know the the wealthier  end of this country who were very big  supporters of Donald Trump in terms of  what he would do to deregulate the  financial industry pro-business reducing  taxes all of that and you know we've  seen some of that coming in already and  with the new tax law what's the American  dream  the American dream I mean I don't know  for Americans but for non-americans fair  and this is what I noticed traveling  around is like there is this insatiable  hope and optimism and positivity to do  better and that your kids will do better  than you did and your grandkids will do  better than you did and when you travel  to America this is the American dream  that's what you hear people describing  to you and you know one person I met I  had had said how you know she was the  first person in her family to finish  high school and she was going to make  sure that her son was the first person  to finish university and she would do  everything she had to do to make sure  that he could be a doctor be a lawyer be  whatever he wanted to be and I think  people are always striving for that and  it's not happening right now in the u.s.  I mean the census statistics show that 3  out of 5 people are the same level of  income and wealth as they were in 2008  like that's quite a substantial period  of time to not be making slight  improvements on your life and and I felt  that people I met particularly those who  had been Democratic voters and Renee's  siding with Donald Trump was they felt  they've been somehow left behind that  they weren't going to retire or die  better off than their parents were and  they weren't going to be able to give a  better life to their children and that  kind of goes against that thinking that  I think is in this spirit  so love Americans what is your reaction  when you hear our politicians say or  even our public say America is the  greatest country in the world I think  you know many people in their own  countries say that in Ireland we say  it's the greatest country in the world  well you know and I mean in many ways  America is is great you know why else do  so many people go through so much to  come here and make a better lot try and  make a better life for themselves and  you know I think and there have been  surveys to back this up in the last few  months that maybe that reputation that  viewpoint is diminishing now and by  virtue of recent policies here things  like not going along with pretty much  every other country on Earth in terms of  the Paris climate record and you know  policies towards the Middle East perhaps  so you know but I think Americans are  entitled to say they're the greatest  country it's the greatest country in the  earth but but so can every other nation  so looking back on your experience of  the four years and looking back on your  work on this book if when you go home  and somebody says to you describe to me  very briefly why the people that voted  for Donald Trump voted for him what  would you say what are the main reasons  I would say there are a couple of  reasons one is he said he would bring  back that American Dream and make life  better for them and that he would change  things up in Washington again the drain  the swamp improved things there and also  because he kind of he didn't stand for  anything in particular he could stand  for anything that you wanted him to  stand for and ultimately a lot of people  are single issue voters but he was  listening to them he said he would fix  the economy and bring back jobs and  ultimately that's what everyone wants in  life you know they want to be able to  provide for themselves and their  families as best they can and if you  feel beaten down you will take a chance  on someone that's offering you something  new so last question to you if you ever  had to come back to the United States  and live again and had a choice which  state would you live in that's the hard  question again I would love to come back  to DC again but again with the job that  I have that you can get out of the  bubble that is the city and travel  around if I was going to check out of  life totally I mean the beaches in  California are pretty amazing and you  know like say Kentucky also a fabulous  place really like Texas I can't I don't  think I could em I have the I've had the  best of both worlds here I've got to  live in a city that lives on politics  which I do but I've got to travel around  every week and visit almost every other  state in this country and meet the great  people and experience what there is to  offer the name of the book is in America  tales from Trump country our guest has  been Katrina Perry and we thank you very  much thanks Bryan
 

